    - Key: nmc.plan.coast
      Value: '{"method":"Pass 9\u2019s: a reference line along the new mean-tide line
        with the land on its left (north); each section is a cross-shore profile,
        blended over `feather` metres along the line; seaward of the last knot the
        ground relaxes to the far floor over `relax` metres. The east coast keeps
        today\u2019s ground (CoastPoints and CoastSectors, NineMileCreekMainland.cs),
        measured here as profiles.","far_floor":{"west":-5,"east":"today\u2019s bay
        (-6.0) by x 200","rule":"floor(x) = lerp(-5.0, -6.0, smoothstep(60, 200, x)),
        then max with the bar\u2019s ridge"},"south_shore":{"id":"coast.nmc_south_shore","name":"the
        south shore","line":[[-380,-203],[-330,-200.5],[-280,-198],[-230,-197],[-180,-197.5],[-130,-196.5],[-85,-193.5],[-45,-189.5],[-5,-184.5],[30,-179.5],[55,-172.5],[74,-166],[88,-159],[85,-150],[80,-140],[75.5,-121],[70,-102]],"feather":14,"relax":60,"runs":"from
        the region\u2019s west edge at (-380, -203), where it carries on into Rice
        Point\u2019s region, east to the landing\u2019s corner at (88, -159), where
        the bar leaves it; then a short hook north along today\u2019s east beach to
        (70, -102), so the corner joins today\u2019s coast","sections":[{"id":"coast.nmc_rice_point_strand","name":"Rice
        Point Strand","type":"sand beach under a low red bank","from":-380,"to":-205,"houses":true,"profile":[[70,6],[46,5.55],[35,5.15],[31,4.2],[27.5,3],[20,2.35],[12,1.5],[6,0.72],[0,0],[-10,-0.6],[-25,-1.3],[-42,-2.2],[-60,-2.9],[-90,-3.7]],"why":"The
        houses stand on the bank top. A red sandstone bank 2 m tall, a storm berm,
        then a wide sand beach whose flats run 42 m out at spring low: clams at low
        water, as at St Peters\u2019 Lagoon Flats."},{"id":"coast.nmc_camp_dunes","name":"the
        camp dunes","type":"sand beach under marram dunes","from":-205,"to":-62,"profile":[[82,6],[58,5.25],[44,4.35],[36,4.75],[31,4.9],[27,3.5],[22,2.55],[14,1.7],[6,0.72],[0,0],[-12,-0.7],[-28,-1.4],[-46,-2.2],[-65,-2.9],[-95,-3.8]],"why":"The
        dune ridge (+4.9) shelters the campground\u2019s south pitches in the swale
        behind it (+4.35). Boardwalks cross it to the beach."},{"id":"coast.nmc_brook_mouth","name":"the
        brook mouth","type":"beach berm with a salt marsh behind","from":-62,"to":-18,"profile":[[72,6],[52,4.1],[40,2.55],[31,2.3],[25,2.65],[19,2.1],[9,0.95],[0,0],[-14,-0.8],[-30,-1.5],[-48,-2.2],[-70,-3],[-95,-3.8]],"why":"The
        camp brook crosses the beach here. A berm (+2.65) holds a little salt marsh
        (+2.3) behind it, drowned only by the spring highs."},{"id":"coast.nmc_landing_beach","name":"the
        landing beach","type":"sand beach, the bar\u2019s root","from":-18,"to":88,"profile":[[27,6],[21,5.45],[15,4.1],[9.5,2.45],[4.5,1],[0,0],[-15,-0.8],[-35,-1.6],[-55,-2.2],[-80,-3],[-110,-3.8]],"why":"Where
        the crossing comes ashore at the corner: the bar\u2019s ridge (+0.88) rises
        out of the beach at (84, -157), and the beach wraps round the corner into
        today\u2019s east beach, north of the landing."}],"rule":"E = profile(d) inland
        of the last seaward knot; beyond it lerp(last, floor, smoothstep(0, relax,
        d_past)); E = max(E, bar ridge); a section\u2019s profile blends into the
        next across `feather` metres of x"},"corner":{"id":"coast.nmc_landing_corner","at":[60,-150],"landing_z":5.2,"bar_road_start_z":5.65,"rule":"north
        of y -118 (and north of the bar\u2019s crest east of x 90) the ground is today\u2019s;
        south of y -138 it is the south shore\u2019s; smoothstep between. The landing
        (60, -150) stays the head of the beach: +5.2 on the plan, 3 m over spring
        high."},"east_coast":{"id":"coast.nmc_east_coast","kept":true,"builder":"NineMileCreekMainland.CoastPoints
        / CoastSectors (unchanged but the south end)","points_today":[[30,-280],[52,-200],[60,-150],[50,-100],[34,-40],[32,20],[44,70],[58,110],[44,128],[26,134],[24,152],[40,168],[34,210],[30,260],[34,280]],"sections":[{"id":"coast.nmc_south_beach_old","cls":"Beach","s":[0,133.6],"from":[30,-280],"to":[60,-150],"fate":"GOES:
        the south shore replaces it; the water comes in over the old fields south
        of the landing"},{"id":"coast.nmc_landing_north_beach","cls":"Beach","s":[133.6,176],"fate":"kept;
        it now runs round the corner into the landing beach"},{"id":"coast.nmc_dune","cls":"Dune","s":[176,210],"fate":"kept"},{"id":"coast.nmc_ledge_bank","cls":"LedgeCliff","s":[210,268],"fate":"kept"},{"id":"coast.nmc_gully","cls":"Access","s":[268,294],"fate":"kept:
        the one way down to the ledges"},{"id":"coast.nmc_weather_face","cls":"Cliff","s":[294,370],"fate":"kept:
        the red bluff, the St Peters sightline"},{"id":"coast.nmc_spit_root","cls":"DeepShoreCliff","s":[370,399],"fate":"kept,
        under the wharf\u2019s west arm as the wharf return drew it"},{"id":"coast.nmc_creek_mouth","cls":"Beach","s":[399,521],"fate":"reshaped
        by the wharf return: the yard and its bank to x 36.5, the barachois\u2019s
        east end back to x 22, the river\u2019s mouth through the bank at (26..48,
        156..170)"},{"id":"coast.nmc_north_dune","cls":"Dune","s":[521,551],"fate":"kept
        but for the north creek\u2019s inlet, which cuts it at y 226..238"},{"id":"coast.nmc_north_beach","cls":"Beach","s":[551,596],"fate":"kept"}]}}'
    - Key: nmc.plan.water
      Value: '{"rule":"water = max(tide, still) (ADR 0046). Each stream\u2019s still
        level is bed + depth along its channel: over its fresh reach, and over its
        tidal reach as the low-water ribbon a river keeps when the tide is out (a
        call, section 7 of the notes). Ponds hold a flat surface. The lagoon and the
        marsh pool are the tide\u2019s.","streams":[{"id":"stream.nmc_town_river","name":"Nine
        Mile Creek (the town river)","joins":["the town river (08-20)","the northern
        waterway (09-28): it is the junction brook\u2019s course carried up through
        the town"],"pts":[[50,162],[40,166],[30,162],[22,154],[10,146],[-8,140],[-28,138],[-48,142],[-66,154],[-84,168],[-96,179],[-110,190],[-122,193],[-134,199],[-146,199.5],[-156,202],[-177,205],[-200,207],[-226,206],[-248,202],[-261,199.5],[-268,198.2],[-273,197.6],[-278.5,197],[-290,199],[-304,204],[-311,209],[-318,211],[-326,216],[-334,216],[-342,212.5],[-350,215],[-366,217],[-380,222]],"z":[-1.2,-1.2,-1.15,-1.1,-1.05,-1,-0.95,-0.9,-0.85,-0.8,-0.75,-0.7,-0.65,-0.6,-0.55,-0.5,-0.4,-0.3,-0.15,0,0.05,-0.35,0.3,2.55,2.62,2.68,2.5,2.36,2.8,2.9,2.98,3.05,3.2,3.35],"w":[12,12,12,12,12,12,12,12,11.5,11,11,11,10.5,10.5,10,10,10,10,9.5,9.5,9.5,11,9,7,6.5,6.5,7,7.5,6.5,6.5,6.5,6.5,6.5,6.5],"depth":[0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.4,0.9,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.5,0.75,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35,0.35],"mouth":{"at":[50,162],"into":"the
        wharf\u2019s creek flats and Nine Mile Creek\u2019s low-water channel along
        the yard\u2019s north side (the wharf return: creekY(x) = 148.5 + 3.2 sin(x/17)
        + 1.4 sin(x/6.3) + 13 ss(146,160,x) ss(196,184,x), bed -1.7), out to the bay
        at x 212"},"head_of_tide":{"at":[-278.5,197],"rule":"the Falls: the bed steps
        from +0.30 to +2.55 over 5.5 m of sandstone ledges; above them the bed stands
        over spring high (+2.2)"},"tidal_reach_m":357,"fresh_reach_m":108,"leaves":{"at":[-380,222],"into":"the
        river\u2019s upper valley in the next region west (not built)"},"banks":{"open":{"mud":4,"upper":5,"note":"outside
        the town: mud banks 1:4 to +2.4, grass 1:5 to the fields"},"town":{"between_x":[-266,-146],"south":{"mud":3,"bench":[2.7,5],"upper":3},"north":{"mud":3,"bench":[2.7,5.5],"wall":6,"fill":"fill.nmc_river_wall
        (in the texture since the re-issue)"},"note":"through the town: a boardwalk
        bench at +2.7 on each bank; the south bank grass 1:3 up to the town (+5.8);
        the north bank a stone retaining wall (it faces south, so the camera sees
        it) up to Water Street (+6.0)"},"fresh":{"bank":2,"floodplain":[1,5],"upper":4,"note":"above
        the Falls: a 1:2 bank to a floodplain meadow 1.0 m over the bed, then 1:4
        to the fields"}},"fishing":["the Falls pool (-268, 198.2): sea-run trout and
        gaspereau at the head of tide","the fresh pool (-318, 211): brook trout","the
        town boardwalks: smelt, striped bass on the flood","the barachois channel
        at the flood"],"why":"The owner\u2019s river off the ocean and up through
        the town. It leaves the barachois by its north-west corner, keeps 55 m or
        more north of the gas bar, crosses Route 91 at (-177, 205) and divides the
        town, then climbs over the Falls into the fields."},{"id":"stream.nmc_town_river_mouth","name":"Nine
